#=GF RM   18922794
#=GF RT   Regulation of the xylan-degrading apparatus of Cellvibrio
#=GF RT   japonicus by a novel two-component system.
#=GF RA   Emami K, Topakas E, Nagy T, Henshaw J, Jackson KA, Nelson KE,
#=GF RA   Mongodin EF, Murray JW, Lewis RJ, Gilbert HJ;
#=GF RL   J Biol Chem. 2009;284:1086-1096.
#=GF DR   INTERPRO; IPR041124;
#=GF DR   SO; 0000417; polypeptide_domain;
#=GF CC   This is the sensor domain of sensor histidine kinase (AbfS)
#=GF CC   present in Cellvibrio japonicus. AbfS forms part of the AbfR/S
#=GF CC   two-component system which is needed to to activate the
#=GF CC   expression of the suite of enzymes that remove the numerous side
#=GF CC   chains from xylan. The overall fold of the sensor domain is that
#=GF CC   of a classical Per Arndt Sim domain [1]. This domain binds
#=GF CC   xylotriose and xylobiose (Matilla et.al, FEMS Microbiology
#=GF CC   Reviews, fuab043, 45, 2021, 1.
#=GF CC   https://doi.org/10.1093/femsre/fuab043).
#=GF SQ   29
